Brute Force: Traverse using two loops , TC: O(N^2)

Better Approach: using hashmap , TC: O(N) and SC: O(N)

Always try to use less space because space is most costier

Optimal Approach: First Sort the Array and then two pointer approach
                  T.C. : O(nlogn) for sorting and for traversing O(n) so O(nlogn) is bigger so T.C.: O(nlogn)  


2) Remove Duplicates from Sorted Array
   ===================================

code: class Solution {
    public int removeDuplicates(int[] nums) {
        int n = nums.length;
        int officer = 0 , cm = 1;
        int res = 1;
        while(cm<n)
        {
            if(nums[cm-1]!=nums[cm]) 
            {
                res++;
                nums[officer+1] = nums[cm];
                officer++;
            }
            cm++;
        }
        return res;
    }
}

T.C. : O(N)

